From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaming Shi <jiaming.shih@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:10:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kselftests-bpf: prevent target flags leaking to host tools

OpenWrt exports empty CFLAGS and LDFLAGS from include/toplevel.mk. The
BPF selftests append SAN_CFLAGS and SAN_LDFLAGS to these variables,
which retain their exported state and are inherited by host tool builds.

After switching target flags from EXTRA_CFLAGS to SAN_CFLAGS, the host
libbpf build receives target compiler flags such as -fhonour-copts. The
native compiler rejects this OpenWrt-specific option, causing the build
to fail.

Unexport CFLAGS and LDFLAGS before invoking the selftests build. Keep
passing target flags through SAN_CFLAGS so target userspace and libbpf
still receive them, without exporting the resulting flags to host tools.

Fixes: 60827c1dc2cd ("kselftests-bpf: isolate target userspace compiler flags")
Signed-off-by: Jiaming Shi <jiaming.shih@gmail.com>
---
 package/devel/kselftests-bpf/Makefile | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/package/devel/kselftests-bpf/Makefile
+++ b/package/devel/kselftests-bpf/Makefile
@@ -42,6 +42,9 @@ MOD_TARGETS:= \
 
 MAKE_PATH:=tools/testing/selftests/bpf
 
+# Keep target flags added by selftests out of the host tool environment.
+unexport CFLAGS LDFLAGS
+
 # Use SAN_CFLAGS to cover target libbpf as well as userspace selftests,
 # without passing target flags to host tools or kernel modules.
 MAKE_VARS:= \
